   - Tile the i-dimension so that each thread works on contiguous bands of
     rows/columns, improving cache locality.
   - Use restrict-qualified local pointers to tell the compiler that u, v, p,
     and q do not alias, enabling better vectorization and scheduling.
   - Hoist loop-invariant scalars and common subexpressions out of inner loops,
     including the “center” coefficients 1 + 2*d and 1 + 2*a.
   - Compute the shared denominator in the forward Thomas sweep once per
     iteration and reuse it for both p and q updates.
