     * Row sweep: solve tridiagonal systems along "rows"
     * (for each fixed i, sweep over j).
     * ============================================================
     *
     * Here we keep the original i-outer/j-inner ordering, which gives
     * good locality for u, v, p, and q along the contiguous j-dimension.
     * We still apply the same denominator-reuse optimization as above.
     */

    /* 1) Left boundary and forward-sweep seeds along each row. */
    for (i = 1; i < _PB_N-1; i++) {
      u[i][0] = SCALAR_VAL(1.0);
      p[i][0] = SCALAR_VAL(0.0);
      q[i][0] = u[i][0]; /* = 1.0 */
    }

